ify, describe\nfacilitate -> enable, help, support\nexemplify -> demonstrate, show, illustrate\nunderscore -> emphasize, highlight\nnavigate -> handle, manage, work with\nstreamline -> simplify, improve, optimize\naugment -> enhance, extend, add to\nbolster -> strengthen, support, reinforce\nspearhead -> lead, drive, initiate\n\n# ============================================================================\n# EMPHATIC OVERUSE - Unnecessary intensifiers\n# ============================================================================\nrealm\nnotable\nprofound -> significant, important, deep\ncrucial -> important, critical, key\nvital -> essential, critical, important\nessential -> necessary, required, needed\nimperative -> necessary, required, critical\nquintessential -> essential, typical, ideal\nindispensable -> necessary, essential, required\ninstrumental -> key, important, helpful\n\n# ============================================================================\n# VAGUE INTENSIFIERS\n# ============================================================================\nsignificantly -> greatly, substantially\nconsiderably -> substantially, greatly\nnotably -> especially, particularly\nmarkedly -> noticeably, clearly\n\n# ============================================================================\n# BUSINESS JARGON\n# ============================================================================\nsynergy -> cooperation, collaboration\nparadigm -> model, framework, approach\ngame-changer -> innovation, advance\ncutting-edge -> advanced, modern, latest\nstate-of-the-art -> advanced, modern, current\nbest-in-class -> leading, top, excellent\nworld-class -> excellent, top-tier\nbest practices -> proven methods, standards\nlow-hanging fruit -> easy wins, quick gains\nmove the needle -> make progress, improve\n\n# ============================================================================\n# HEDGING AND FILLER PHRASES\n# ==========================================================